# Field UI

Used one-handed, standing on a doorstep, often in rain, often with no signal.

- Minimum 44px tap targets. Primary actions bottom-anchored within thumb reach.
- NO scoring, ranking, colour-coding or quality signal of any kind. This is architectural — canvassers who can see which doors score well will cherry-pick, and the coverage data stops meaning anything.
- Every write goes through `lib/sync/queue.ts`. No direct Supabase calls in field components.
  - Exception (UI-7): the live position RPCs in `lib/field/position-share.ts`. See rule 30-sync and the `geo-position` skill.
- Every screen must be usable in airplane mode from the cached assignment snapshot.
- Stale data is shown greyed with its age. Never render a stale value as if it were live.
- A door's identity is its UPRN. There is no address text, house number or autocomplete.
- Optimistic UI: a logged knock changes state immediately, before sync confirms.